.TH "CSSIMAGEVALUE" "3JS" "August 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSImageValue \- CSSImageValue
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSImageValue\f[B]\f[R] interface of the CSS Typed Object
Model API represents values for CSS properties that take an
\f[CR]image\f[R] value, such as \f[CR]background\-image\f[R],
\f[CR]list\-style\-image\f[R], or \f[CR]border\-image\-source\f[R].
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
None.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]Also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSStyleValue\f[I].\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[CR]CSSImageValue\f[R] can contain every kind of value the
\f[CR]image\f[R] data type accepts, including URL\-based images
specified using \f[CR]url()\f[R], \f[CR]gradient\f[R]s such as
\f[CR]linear\-gradient()\f[R], \f[CR]image()\f[R],
\f[CR]image\-set()\f[R], \f[CR]cross\-fade()\f[R], and
\f[CR]element()\f[R].
.PP
For image values that involve a URL, such as \f[CR]url()\f[R] or
\f[CR]image()\f[R], relative and fragment URLs are resolved the same way
as in CSS.
That is, relative to the style sheet\(cqs URL, or the document\(cqs URL
for inline styles.
.PP
This resolution happens during value computation rather than at parse
time, which means that the value of a \f[CR]CSSImageValue\f[R] depends
on whether you\(cqre working with the specified value or the computed
value:
.IP \(bu 2
A \f[B]specified\f[R] value carries an unresolved relative URL.
If the unresolved value is copied to an element in a different document,
it resolves against the destination document\(cqs own base URL and can
point to a different resource.
.IP \(bu 2
A \f[B]computed\f[R] value has already been resolved to an absolute URL,
so it behaves consistently no matter which document it\(cqs later
applied to.
.IP \(bu 2
A \f[B]fragment\-only\f[R] URL value is always resolved against the
current document.
.PP
Note that \f[CR]CSSImageValue\f[R] objects are intentionally opaque:
they don\(cqt expose any information about the image they represent.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example sets the \f[CR]background\-image\f[R] of a
\f[CR]<button>\f[R] using \f[CR]url()\f[R], specifying a relative URL
for the file.
We then demonstrate getting the stringified computed and specified
values.
.PP
Note that there is hidden logging code that is not shown, as it is not
relevant to the example.
.SS HTML
First we define the button element:
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]button\f[R]>Magic Wand</\f[B]button\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
We add some CSS, including a background image requesting a binary file:
.IP
.EX
button {
  \f[B]display\f[R]: inline\-block;
  \f[B]min\-height\f[R]: 100px;
  \f[B]min\-width\f[R]: 100px;
  \f[B]background\f[R]: no\-repeat 5% center url(\(dqmagic\-wand.png\(dq) aqua;
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
Next we get the \f[CR]<button>\f[R] element so that we can query its
specified and computed styles.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// get the element\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] button = document.querySelector(\(dqbutton\(dq);
.EE
.PP
To get the computed value of the \f[CR]background\-image\f[R] we first
get the element\(cqs style map.
Then we \f[CR]get()\f[R] the \f[CR]background\-image\f[R] from the style
map and stringify it.
We also print the name of the constructor to demonstrate the returned
object is a \f[CR]CSSImageValue\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Get all computed styles with computedStyleMap()\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] allComputedStyles = button.computedStyleMap();
\f[B]const\f[R] computedImageCSS = allComputedStyles.get(\(dqbackground\-image\(dq);
log(computedImageCSS.toString());
log(computedImageCSS.constructor.name); \f[I]// CSSImageValue\f[R]
.EE
.PP
Next we get the specified value of the \f[CR]background\-image\f[R].
To do this we first get the set of CSS rules associated with the
\f[CR]css\-output\f[R] element \(em this is where MDN writes CSS for the
playground.
We then filter the rule to find the CSS rule matched purely on its name
\(lqbutton\(rq (note, this is fragile code in a real application).
Once we have the associated rule we can get the image from its style
map, and log the value.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Get the specified value\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] sheet = document.getElementById(\(dqcss\-output\(dq).sheet;
\f[B]const\f[R] rule = [...sheet.cssRules].find((r) \f[B]=>\f[R] r.selectorText === \(dqbutton\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] specifiedImageCSS = rule.styleMap.get(\(dqbackground\-image\(dq);
log(specifiedImageCSS.toString());
log(specifiedImageCSS.constructor.name); \f[I]// CSSImageValue\f[R]
.EE
.SS Result
The results are shown below.
Note that the computed value displayed first has a fully resolved URL,
while the specified value is a relative URL.
